IO-12: keep the Geom3 size code of ellipse and arch pipes; reject non-whole codes

For HORIZ_ELLIPSE, VERT_ELLIPSE and ARCH, xsect_setParams() took Geom1 as the
size code whenever Geom2 was 0 (the SWMM 5.0 input form), even when Geom3
held a size code, and truncated any size code to a whole number. A line that
gives the full height and the size code but leaves the width to the code
("HORIZ_ELLIPSE 2 0 4") was built as a different standard pipe (code 2), a
custom height with the width left out ("HORIZ_ELLIPSE 1.2 0 0" in metres)
became standard size 1, and "ARCH 4.5 7.0 12.5" became code 12. Apply the 5.0
form only when Geom3 is 0, and reject a size code that is not a whole number.
5.0-form lines with whole codes ("HORIZ_ELLIPSE 17 0 0") are read as before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-12_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c b/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c
index cf40f97..4445bfd 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c
@@ -554,11 +554,11 @@ int xsect_setParams(TXsect *xsect, int type, double p[], double ucf)
         break;
 
     case HORIZ_ELLIPSE:
-        if ( p[1] == 0.0 ) p[2] = p[0];
+        if ( p[1] == 0.0 && p[2] == 0.0 ) p[2] = p[0];  // SWMM 5.0 format
         if ( p[2] > 0.0 )                        // std. ellipse pipe
         {
             index = (int)floor(p[2]) - 1;        // size code
-            if ( index < 0 ||
+            if ( index < 0 || index + 1 != p[2] ||
                  index >= NumCodesEllipse ) return FALSE;
             xsect->yFull = MinorAxis_Ellipse[index]/12.;
             xsect->wMax  = MajorAxis_Ellipse[index]/12.;
@@ -582,11 +582,11 @@ int xsect_setParams(TXsect *xsect, int type, double p[], double ucf)
         break;
 
     case VERT_ELLIPSE:
-        if ( p[1] == 0.0 ) p[2] = p[0];
+        if ( p[1] == 0.0 && p[2] == 0.0 ) p[2] = p[0];  // SWMM 5.0 format
         if ( p[2] > 0.0 )                        // std. ellipse pipe
         {
             index = (int)floor(p[2]) - 1;        // size code
-            if ( index < 0 ||
+            if ( index < 0 || index + 1 != p[2] ||
                  index >= NumCodesEllipse ) return FALSE;
             xsect->yFull = MajorAxis_Ellipse[index]/12.;
             xsect->wMax  = MinorAxis_Ellipse[index]/12.;
@@ -610,11 +610,11 @@ int xsect_setParams(TXsect *xsect, int type, double p[], double ucf)
         break;
 
     case ARCH:
-        if ( p[1] == 0.0 ) p[2] = p[0];
+        if ( p[1] == 0.0 && p[2] == 0.0 ) p[2] = p[0];  // SWMM 5.0 format
         if ( p[2] > 0.0 )                        // std. arch pipe
         {
             index = (int)floor(p[2]) - 1;        // size code
-            if ( index < 0 ||
+            if ( index < 0 || index + 1 != p[2] ||
                  index >= NumCodesArch ) return FALSE;
             xsect->yFull = Yfull_Arch[index]/12.;     // Yfull units are inches
             xsect->wMax  = Wmax_Arch[index]/12.;      // Wmax units are inches
